# CVE ignores require a dated justification and an owner to re-check.
#
# 2026-07-29 (#853) re-check: three of the four entries here were retired by
# bumping the dependency. What they had been suppressed FOR did not survive
# verification — the recorded reason ("the fixed version is published without
# provenance attestation while earlier versions had it, so pnpm's
# trustPolicy: no-downgrade refuses the upgrade") was checked against the npm
# registry and was false: NO published version of brace-expansion (0 of 44) or
# fast-uri (0 of 29) has EVER carried a provenance attestation, so there was no
# downgrade to refuse. For postcss the truth ran the other way — the pinned
# 8.5.16 was unattested and every fix version (8.5.18+) IS attested, so the
# bump strengthened provenance. The companion claim that the lockfile "predates
# the tightened pnpm policy so ANY install refuses" was also false:
# `pnpm@11.0.0 install --frozen-lockfile` succeeds against the committed
# lockfile as-is.
#
# Re-check procedure (run it, do not re-derive it): compare
# `registry.npmjs.org/<pkg>/<version>` `.dist.attestations` for the pinned and
# the fixed version before believing any provenance-based suppression.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 — react-router CSRF bypass, HIGH.
# Advisory: vulnerable >=7.12.0 <8.3.0, first patched 8.3.0 (published
# 2026-07-24). Pinned: react-router 7.18.1.
#
# Upstream status 2026-07-29: 8.3.0 IS published and IS provenance-attested, so
# unlike the other three this is NOT blocked on upstream — it is blocked on a
# breaking 7 -> 8 major of the admin SPA's router. Upstream shipped no 7.x
# backport: 7.18.2 exists and does NOT carry the fix.
#
# Why the suppression still holds: the bypass is reachable only in react-router
# RSC mode. web/admin is a Vite SPA (react-router-dom 7.18.1, browser router);
# RSC is never enabled, so no vulnerable code path is built or served, and the
# console bundle is build-time output rather than a served dependency.
#
# This has a re-check TRIGGER, not an expiry date: it dies the moment web/admin
# adopts RSC, or a react-router 7.x patch appears. Owner: openrails tracker #853.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2
